.TH XNVME-CMD-ADMIN 1 "14 October 2026" "xNVMe" "xNVMe"
.SH NAME
\fBxnvme-cmd-admin \fP- An admin command, as 'nvme admin-passthru' takes it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.fam C
\fBxnvme\fP \fIcmd-admin\fP <uri> [\fIOPTIONS\fP]
.fam T
.fi
.fam T
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Send a user-defined command to the device at <uri>, any xNVMe URI: a character or block device, a BDF, or a fabrics address. The options are those of nvme admin-passthru, with the same names and letters:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    -O, --opcode=NUM       -f, --flags=NUM        -p, --prefill=NUM
    -R, --rsvd=NUM         -n, --namespace-id=NUM -l, --data-len=NUM
    -m, --metadata-len=NUM -2, --cdw2=NUM         -3, --cdw3=NUM
    -4 .. -9, --cdw10=NUM .. --cdw15=NUM          -i, --input-file=FILE
    -M, --metadata=FILE    -b, --raw-binary       -s, --show-command
    -d, --dry-run          -r, --read             -w, --write
    -T, --latency          -t, --timeout=NUM      -o, --output-format=FMT
    -v, --verbose          --no-retries

.fam T
.fi
and, choosing the path: \fB--be\fP, \fB--admin\fP, \fB--sync\fP, \fB--async\fP, \fB--dev-nsid\fP and \fB--homi-id\fP or \fB--shm_id\fP.
.RE
.PP


